  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nChrome stops pending `javascript:` navigations when a form [plans to navigate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#plan-to-navigate) during submission: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/forms/html_form_element.cc;l=1017;drc=0579e62a02d9160f6953550caa2d1639742abeaa?q=form_element.cc&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc.\nThere is a WPT which expects this behaviour, and all browsers currently pass ([jsurl-navigation-then-form-submit.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/forms/form-submission-0/jsurl-navigation-then-form-submit.html?label=experimental&label=master&aligned)) but it's not in the specification.\n(Gecko currently does form submission synchronously, which has the same effect, although we are now trying to align with the spec and make it asynchronous and have run into this issue.)",
